      <p>Security in practice</p>

      <h2 id="security-overview-title">
        Security is a condition to maintain, not a feature to install.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="security-overview__copy">
      <p>
        Business systems change continuously. New users are added,
        dependencies are updated, services are exposed, credentials
        are created and infrastructure evolves.
      </p>

      <p>
        Those changes can gradually create risks that were not
        present when the system was first deployed.
      </p>

      <p>
        A practical security approach combines prevention,
        maintenance, controlled access, backup readiness and
        the ability to recover when something does go wrong.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
